<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			10/7/97		   3/7/97	     12/7/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	375-400			425		   400</p>
<p>    Naphtha	  75-100		   75-100		    50</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,850	    1,850-1,900	 1,475-1,500</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	    300		  275-300	     375-400</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     15			 15		 10-15</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks dipped with the departure of barges to Germany and as cargoes to both northwest Europe and the Med.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks were barely changed with no major movements.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks came off slightly with much transhipment. Some cargoes arrived from Russia and the Med, while barges exited down the Rhine.</p>
<p>Fuel oil inventories rose slightly with incoming barges and straight-run product. Some VGO left for Germany.</p>
<p>Jet fuel levels were steady. Some went to the aviation sector.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
</text>
